-- ============================================================================
-- D1 EXPERT DEEP SEED: Oilfield Data Quality, advanced tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed, and the question rows from the
-- committed bank JSONs under tools/course-banks/dataqc/advanced.
--
-- What this tier owns: HAS THE PROCESS CHANGED, AND WHAT IS THE POLICY. The
-- individuals and moving range chart with d2 and D4 as NIST prints them; EWMA
-- with target and sigma from in-control history, asymptotic and exact limits;
-- the tabular CUSUM with k and h in a stated unit and no reset; the scorecard
-- with weights normalised by their sum, the weakest dimension and no grade
-- bands; the Petrolord defaults presented as choices and the order of checks;
-- the NIST printed-figure errata and what the engine does not build. Digest
-- sections 25 to 31, and section 32.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. A chart drawn on the data it monitors absorbs
-- the shift it is looking for, and a small shift is seen by EWMA and CUSUM and
-- missed by the individuals chart. The Expert capstone grades phase-one
-- limits, EWMA, CUSUM and a weighted scorecard.
-- ============================================================================

values ('dataqc', 'advanced', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-individuals-chart","title":"The Individuals Chart","lesson_keys":["l01-a-process-that-makes-data","l02-the-moving-range","l03-limits-from-the-moving-range","l04-the-moving-range-chart","l05-a-standard-or-the-data"]},{"key":"m02-the-ewma-chart","title":"The EWMA Chart","lesson_keys":["l01-a-weighted-memory","l02-target-and-sigma-from-history","l03-asymptotic-and-exact-limits","l04-choosing-lambda"]},{"key":"m03-the-tabular-cusum","title":"The Tabular CUSUM","lesson_keys":["l01-accumulating-small-shifts","l02-k-and-h-in-stated-units","l03-no-reset-after-a-signal","l04-the-nist-table-and-its-design","l05-which-chart-sees-what"]},{"key":"m04-the-scorecard","title":"The Scorecard","lesson_keys":["l01-a-score-per-dimension","l02-weights-and-their-normalisation","l03-the-weakest-dimension","l04-why-there-are-no-grade-bands"]},{"key":"m05-designing-a-qc-policy","title":"Designing a QC Policy","lesson_keys":["l01-the-order-of-checks","l02-defaults-are-choices","l03-flag-fix-or-refuse","l04-writing-the-policy"]},{"key":"m06-reading-the-engine-honestly","title":"Reading the Engine Honestly","lesson_keys":["l01-printed-figures-and-their-errata","l02-what-is-not-built","l03-writing-the-quality-note","l04-the-capstone-brief"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
